{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOver the MCP server, `claim_ticket` (`src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:300-318`) calls `rebar.claim`, whose claim event stamps `(\"session\", resolve_session_id())` and `(\"harness\", resolve_harness())` from the **server process's** environment (`src/rebar/_commands/txn.py:71-72`, resolver at `src/rebar/_commands/session_id.py:63`). On the AWS deployment those variables describe the server, not the calling agent, so every MCP-driven claim records no usable `claimed_session`, and `cross_session_warning_for` (`src/rebar/_commands/cross_session.py:45`) is silent for every MCP caller. The inbox feed (the dependent child) needs a recipient identity that exists on the mandated MCP path.\n\n## Approach\n\nResolve an **MCP acting-session identity** on the server as `principal` + optional `session_hint`, scoped so a client can never select another principal's identity.\n\n- **Principal seam (all auth strategies)**: the MCP SDK's `mcp.server.auth.middleware.auth_context.get_access_token()` — a request-scoped ContextVar that `AuthContextMiddleware` populates, and `FastMCP.streamable_http_app()` installs that middleware whenever a token verifier is configured (rebar passes its composite verifier at `src/rebar/mcp_server.py:615`). Every rebar verifier returns `AccessToken(client_id=...)`: static PAT (`src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py:209-220`), JWKS (`:332`), introspection (`:504`), proxy (`:147`, which itself reads `PROXY_IDENTITY`). So `principal = get_access_token().client_id` at tool-call time, one PAT per harness per `docs/mcp-client-setup.md:25-27`.\n- **Hint seam**: a new request header `X-Rebar-Session-Id`, captured by a new `SessionHintMiddleware` in `_mcp_auth.py` into a new ContextVar `MCP_SESSION_HINT`. It is wired for **every** strategy by wrapping `mcp.streamable_http_app` with the same method-assignment pattern the proxy guard uses (`src/rebar/mcp_server.py:628-638`) but unconditionally, outside the `proxy`-only branch. It only records the hint — it never authenticates. Validation: ≤128 chars, `[A-Za-z0-9._:-]`; anything else is treated as absent. The transport `Mcp-Session-Id` is deliberately not a fallback (it churns on reconnect and blue-green cutover, bug `aca0-6a66-0a27-47cf`).\n- **Resolver**: `current_mcp_identity() -> (principal, hint) | None` in `_mcp_auth.py`; `resolve_session_id()` gains one higher-precedence source ahead of `REBAR_SESSION_ID` that imports it lazily inside the function (the pattern `cross_session.py:40-43` uses), returning `mcp:<principal>` or `mcp:<principal>/<hint>`; `resolve_harness()` returns `mcp:<principal>`. With no MCP request context both ContextVars are unset and CLI/library behavior is byte-identical to today.\n- **Consumers of the resolver (all enumerated)**: `txn.py:71` claim stamp — migrated (the whole point); `cross_session.py:45` — migrated, the warning now fires over MCP with no reducer change because `_fold_claimed_session` (`src/rebar/reducer/_processors_status.py:25`) stores the string; `session_log.py:58/151/184` — the server-side session-log pointer now rotates per MCP identity instead of one shared log, an accepted and documented effect; `transition_close.py:785` — the FORCE_CLOSE audit string now reads `mcp:<principal>[/<hint>]` over MCP, cosmetic, accepted; `_cli/_llm_commands.py:172` — CLI-only, never has MCP context, unaffected.\n- **Client recipes** (`docs/mcp-client-setup.md`, the three supported clients only): Claude Code — `headers: {\"X-Rebar-Session-Id\": \"${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID}\"}` beside the existing `Authorization: Bearer ${MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLAUDE}`; Codex — `env_http_headers = { \"X-Rebar-Session-Id\" = \"REBAR_SESSION_ID\" }` (the Codex config reference documents `env_http_headers` as headers populated from named env vars), principal-only unless the operator sets that variable, since Codex exposes no per-session variable (`session_id.py:31-33`); Copilot — principal-only in v1 (no per-session variable). Documented degradation: without a hint, all sessions of one principal share `mcp:<principal>`.\n\nPositive rationale: the SDK already carries the accepted principal per request, and the proxy guard already shows how rebar wraps the ASGI app — reusing both adds no auth path and no store schema change (`claimed_session`/`claim_harness` are existing nullable strings). Riskiest assumption, tested first: that Claude Code expands `${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID}` in an HTTP header at connect time (open bugs anthropics/claude-code#6204 and #51581 concern header substitution). Step 1 is a throwaway probe against the deployed server with a temporary debug log line reading the hint back; its verdict is recorded on this ticket and decides whether the Claude Code recipe ships as supported or as principal-only. Rollout/rollback: the change is additive (older server writes null, newer writes the composite; the detector handles both), so old and new images coexist during the blue-green cutover and rollback is redeploying the previous image with no data cleanup.\n\nFailure disposition: a malformed or over-long hint is dropped (identity degrades to `mcp:<principal>`), never an error — the header is advisory sub-partitioning, not authentication.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py` — `MCP_SESSION_HINT`, `SessionHintMiddleware`, `current_mcp_identity()`.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/session_id.py` — MCP source ahead of the env-var chain in `resolve_session_id()` / `resolve_harness()`.\n- `src/rebar/mcp_server.py` — unconditional wrap of `streamable_http_app` with `SessionHintMiddleware`.\n- `docs/mcp-client-setup.md` (Claude Code and Codex recipes; Copilot principal-only), `docs/mcp-auth.md` (header semantics: advisory, principal-scoped, never authenticating), `docs/session-id-shims.md` (correct the stale \"`CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` is remote-only\" note — the local CLI exports it in 2.1.x), `docs/event-schema.md` (the `mcp:<principal>[/<hint>]` value shape of `claimed_session`; the session-log pointer effect).\n- `tests/unit/test_session_id.py`, `tests/unit/test_mcp_auth.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_claim_session.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\n- Unit (pure): `resolve_session_id()` precedence matrix — MCP context with/without hint, malformed hint, no MCP context → env chain unchanged (negative control: existing cases pass unmodified).\n- Unit (middleware): `SessionHintMiddleware` sets the ContextVar for a valid header, leaves it unset for absent/over-long/bad-charset, and is installed regardless of auth strategy (static, jwks, proxy).\n- Contract (the tier that crosses both middlewares + tool + reducer): drive the real ASGI app from `mcp.streamable_http_app()` through `httpx.ASGITransport` with `Authorization: Bearer <static PAT>` and `X-Rebar-Session-Id`, so `AuthContextMiddleware` and `SessionHintMiddleware` both run; `claim_ticket` then `show_ticket` reports `claimed_session == \"mcp:<client_id>/<hint>\"` and `claim_harness == \"mcp:<client_id>\"`; a second request under the same PAT with a different hint calling `comment_ticket` receives a non-null `cross_session_warning`; the same hint → null (contrast).\n- Gate: all under `make test`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A `claim_ticket` over the MCP ASGI app records `claimed_session` as `mcp:<client_id>/<hint>` when `X-Rebar-Session-Id` is sent and `mcp:<client_id>` when it is not; verified by `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_claim_session.py`.\n- [ ] `comment_ticket` over MCP from a different hint under the same PAT returns a non-null `cross_session_warning`, and the same hint returns null; verified by the contrast test in the same file.\n- [ ] A hint longer than 128 chars or outside `[A-Za-z0-9._:-]` is ignored and the claim still records `mcp:<client_id>`; verified by `tests/unit/test_mcp_auth.py`.\n- [ ] `SessionHintMiddleware` is present on the app under the static, jwks, and proxy strategies; verified by `tests/unit/test_mcp_auth.py`.\n- [ ] Outside an MCP request, `resolve_session_id()` output is unchanged for every existing env-var case; verified by `tests/unit/test_session_id.py`.\n- [ ] `docs/event-schema.md` documents the `mcp:<principal>[/<hint>]` value shape and the per-identity session-log pointer effect, and `docs/mcp-auth.md` documents the header as advisory and principal-scoped; verified by a grep assertion in `tests/unit/test_mcp_auth.py`.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The header-expansion probe verdict for Claude Code (expands / does not expand, harness version, timestamp) is recorded as a comment on this ticket before the Claude Code recipe is marked supported in `docs/mcp-client-setup.md`.\n- [ ] `docs/session-id-shims.md` no longer states that `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` is exposed only in the remote runner; verified by the docs-drift gate."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788562661693400001,"uuid":"d45270ee-a13b-4060-9bde-1c005a25afb7"}